  "status_text": "Eleven reports can say anything you like. A twelfth can expose a contradiction that every smaller set misses. Lean checked a construction with two reporting sensors and twelve inputs around a cycle. Each input picks a view for each sensor, and the report is the odd-or-even sum of their answers. One pair of fixed rules fits all twelve requested report bits exactly when their total is even. Every smaller set can be fitted for any requested bits. An odd full cycle therefore needs all twelve reports to witness the failure (L-lib-1105).",
